  6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

  You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the machine-readable
Corresponding Source under the terms of this License, in one of these
ways:

    a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
    (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
    Corresponding Source fixed on a durable medium customarily used
    for software exchange.

    b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
    (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
    written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
    long as you offer spare parts or customer support for that product,
    to give anyone who possesses the object code either (1) a copy of
    the Corresponding Source for a machine-readable software product
    that is installed on a physical product, or (2) a copy of the
    Corresponding Source for a machine-readable software product that
    is distributed on a network server, or (3) a copy of the
    Corresponding Source for a machine-readable software product that
    is distributed via a network server, at no charge except the cost
    of physically performing this distribution.

    c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a written offer
    to provide the Corresponding Source.  This alternative is allowed
    only occasionally and noncommercially, and only if you received the
    object code with such an offer, in accord with subsection 6b.

    d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
    place (gratis or for a fee), and offer equivalent access to the
    Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
    further charge.  You need not require recipients to copy the
    Corresponding Source along with the object code.  If the place to
    obtain the object code is a network server, the Corresponding
    Source may be on a different server (operated by the same party or
    by a third party) that you maintain, provided you give clear
    instructions on where to find the Corresponding Source.  Regardless
    of what server hosts the Corresponding Source, you remain responsible
    for ensuring that the Corresponding Source is available.

    e) Convey the object code by peer-to-peer transmission, provided
    you inform other peers where the object code is available and how
    to view the Corresponding Source.

  A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is excluded
from the Corresponding Source as a System Library, need not be
included in the Corresponding Source.

  A "User Product" is either (1) a "consumer product", which means any
